content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Bettor",
      "description": "person who places bets on match outcomes"
    },
    {
      "name": "Bet",
      "description": "record of a wager placed on a specific match outcome"
    },
    {
      "name": "Match",
      "description": "sporting event with a predicted outcome and final result"
    },
    {
      "name": "Predicted Outcome",
      "description": "expected result of a match used for betting decisions"
    },
    {
      "name": "Result",
      "description": "final outcome of a match after it concludes"
    },
    {
      "name": "Oddsmaker",
      "description": "specialist who analyzes data to set and adjust betting odds"
    },
    {
      "name": "Performance Statistics",
      "description": "analytical data describing team or player performance"
    },
    {
      "name": "Bookmaker",
      "description": "entity that accepts bets and manages wager records"
    },
    {
      "name": "Winning",
      "description": "payout owed to a bettor when a bet succeeds"
    },
    {
      "name": "Wager",
      "description": "amount staked by a bettor when placing a bet"
    },
    {
      "name": "Risk Manager",
      "description": "analyst who evaluates betting exposure to control risk"
    },
    {
      "name": "Data Trends",
      "description": "patterns in betting activity or performance data used for evaluation"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Betting": {
      "objects": [
        "Bettor",
        "Bet",
        "Match",
        "Result",
        "Predicted Outcome"
      ]
    },
    "Statistics": {
      "objects": [
        "Oddsmaker",
        "Performance Statistics",
        "Match",
        "Predicted Outcome"
      ]
    },
    "Bookmaking": {
      "objects": [
        "Bookmaker",
        "Winning",
        "Wager",
        "Risk Manager",
        "Data Trends"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Betting": {
      "derived from": "Betting Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Bettor",
        "Bet",
        "Match",
        "Result",
        "Betting Odds"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Predicted Outcome -> Betting Odds"
      ]
    },
    "Statistics": {
      "derived from": "Statistics Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Oddsmaker",
        "Performance Statistics",
        "Match Record",
        "Outcome Prediction"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Match -> Match Record",
        "Predicted Outcome -> Outcome Prediction"
      ]
    },
    "Bookmaking": {
      "derived from": "Bookmaking Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Bookmaker",
        "Winning",
        "Wager",
        "Risk Manager",
        "Data Trends"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    }
  }
}
```
